CREATE TABLE public.counselor_private_profiles (key text PRIMARY KEY, content text NOT NULL, updated_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now());
GRANT ALL ON public.counselor_private_profiles TO service_role;
ALTER TABLE public.counselor_private_profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
INSERT INTO public.counselor_private_profiles (key, content) VALUES ('april_chart', $p$April — born September 6, 1990, 3:38 PM EDT, Geneva, New York (42°52′N 76°59′W). Age 35, 12th-house profection year, Personal Year 7 in 2026.
Placements: Sun Virgo 13°56′ 8th house · Moon Aries 6°37′ 3rd house (bucket-chart handle) · Mercury Virgo 16°35′ 8th, retrograde, domicile · Venus Leo 29°20′ 8th, anaretic · Mars Gemini 3°02′ 5th · Jupiter Leo 3°59′ 7th (chart ruler) · Saturn Capricorn 18°55′ 1st, retrograde, domicile · Uranus Capricorn 5°37′ 1st, retrograde · Neptune Capricorn 11°52′ 1st, retrograde · Pluto Scorpio 15°28′ 10th, domicile, most elevated · Chiron Cancer 24°30′ 7th · North Node Aquarius 5°17′ 1st / South Node Leo 7th · Vertex Leo 10°38′ 8th · Black Moon Lilith Sagittarius 4°16′ 11th · Part of Fortune Cancer 22°08′ 7th.
Angles: Ascendant Sagittarius 29°28′ (anaretic, near the Galactic Center) · source-reported Midheaven Libra 24°59′ conjunct Spica.
Verified major planet-to-planet aspects from the recorded degrees: Mars sextile Jupiter (0°57′) · Moon square Uranus (1°00′) · Mercury sextile Pluto (1°06′) · Sun sextile Pluto (1°32′) · Sun trine Neptune (2°04′) · Mercury trine Saturn (2°20′) · Moon trine Jupiter (2°38′) · Sun conjunct Mercury (2°38′) · Saturn sextile Pluto (3°27′) · Moon sextile Mars (3°35′) · Neptune sextile Pluto (3°36′) · Venus square Mars (3°42′) · Mercury trine Neptune (4°43′) · Sun trine Saturn (4°58′). The source calls this a Full Moon chart, but the stated Sun and Moon are 157.3° apart, a waning gibbous phase rather than a standard opposition.
Other systems: Life Path 7 · Chinese Metal Horse · Kua 1 (Water) per her Feng Shui guide.$p$),
('april_psychology', $p$How this chart tends to function (use as working hypotheses, always checked against what she tells you):
- Sun–Moon contrast (Virgo Sun 8th and Aries Moon 3rd): a fast, honest emotional spark that wants to be spoken now alongside a careful, private analyser who wants to get it exactly right. This is a useful psychological contrast, not a calculated opposition.
- Aries Moon: feelings arrive hot and quick and pass quickly; she needs to act or voice them. Responds best to directness, momentum and a concrete next step; feels smothered by slow, vague or over-cautious replies.
- Virgo Sun + retrograde Mercury in the 8th: deep, private processing, re-thinking conversations afterward, high standards, a loud inner critic, loyalty expressed through practical help. Responds to precision, structure, specifics and usefulness; is put off by fluff.
- Moon square Uranus, three source-placed planets in the 8th: quick reactions when freedom feels threatened, deep trust themes and a need for safety before going inward.
- Venus square Mars, Venus anaretic in Leo 8th: warmth and loyalty can rub against a need for variety and direct action; attraction works best when affection and independence both have room.
- Capricorn stack in the 1st (Saturn, Uranus, Neptune): carries responsibility early, seems older than her age, self-reliant, can hide softness behind competence. Respect her competence; never patronise.
- Chiron Cancer 7th + South Node Leo 7th: old wound around being cared for in partnership; tends to over-give or over-perform for love. North Node Aquarius 1st: growth is towards owning her own unusual path and independence.
- Sagittarius 29° Ascendant: meets life looking for meaning, truth and freedom; humour and a big-picture frame open her up.
- Pluto most elevated in Scorpio 10th, Jupiter chart ruler in the 7th: power and reinvention through her work and public life; growth through other people.$p$),
('april_context_rules', $p$Accuracy and memory rules:
- Use April's verified birth data and placements above as the stable reference. Never invent a placement, aspect, event, diagnosis, relative, surname, ancestor, family lineage or childhood story.
- Goble and LeCompte ancestry claims are incorrect and must never be repeated. Do not infer any specific family history from the 4th, 8th or 12th houses, Cancer, Chiron, nodes, Sabian symbols or source metaphors.
- When discussing Family & Home, stay with chart-specific symbolism: Pisces on the 4th-house cusp, Neptune in Capricorn in the 1st as ruler, the Aries Moon in the 3rd, and April's source-led Kua 1 home directions. Clearly label interpretation as a possibility, not biography.
- Treat all prior messages in the current saved conversation as durable context. Carry forward April's stated preferences, corrections, goals, boundaries and outcomes; if new information conflicts with an older assumption, use the correction. Do not claim to remember other sessions unless that content is present here.
- Be broadly expert but honest about scope: astrology and April's chart; evidence-informed psychology and therapy skills; life organisation; emotional regulation; communication, relationships and social coaching. Distinguish chart symbolism, research evidence, clinical guidance and personal inference. Never present symbolic systems as science.$p$);